  "display": {
    "case_id": "188721101",
    "target_stage": "Landlord's appeal under Section 38 of the Delhi Rent Control Act from the CCJ-cum-ARC judgment dated 15.03.2019.",
    "target_court": "Principal District & Sessions Judge (Central), Tis Hazari Courts, Delhi",
    "records": [
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L72:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L72:span1": [
            227,
            440
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "188721101",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "2. It was the case of the eviction petitioner - landlord that she had rented out the premises bearing Shop No. 15, in property no. 4415, Gali Bahuji, Pahari Dheeraj, Delhi-110006 to one Sh. Ramesh Kumar on 06.01.1987. However, the said tenant Sh. Ramesh Kumar had parted with possession and sub-let and assigned the same initially to one Sh. Ghanshyam Dass and subsequently to Sh. Bhagwan Dass, who were his father and brother respectively."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L73:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L73:span2": [
            0,
            115
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "188721101",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "The current sub-lessee Bhagwant Dass was pleaded to be opening and closing the shop and dealing with the customers. It was also pleaded that the aforesaid Sh. Bhagwan Dass was a tenant in his independent rights of the petitioner in shop no. 6 in the same property and was using the shop no. 6 as godown and had shifted the counter from shop no. 6 to shop no. 15. Necessary permission for institution of eviction petition from the competent Slum Authority had been taken."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L74:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L74:span3": [
            78,
            162
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "188721101",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "2.1 Petition was resisted by present respondent - tenant Sh. Ramesh Kumar and it was denied that the property had been sub let by him to his brother Bhagwan Dass. It was pleaded by the respondent that he is occupying the demised shop as a tenant and additionally conducting his business from shop no. 5765, Sikli Gran, Factory Road, Nabi Karim, New Delhi-110055."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L75:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L75:span4": [
            93,
            281
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "188721101",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "As regards the respondent's brother Bhagwan Dass, it was further case of the respondent that his brother Bhagwan Dass was helping him in opening and closing the shop and dealing with the customers. However, it was denied that Sh. Bhagwan Dass was a sub tenant in the suit premises. Petitioner was pleaded to be receiving rent from the respondent."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L80:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L80:span5": [
            214,
            320
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "188721101",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "3. Petitioner in support of her case examined her attorney, Sh. M.L. Jain as PW-1, who supported the petition. Petitioner also examined two other witnesses, who were shopkeepers having their shops in the vicinity. Both the witnesses deposed that Sh. Bhagwan Dass was running the shop and not respondent Sh. Ramesh Kumar."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L81:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L81:span6": [
            129,
            252
          ],
          "IK-188721101:L81:span7": [
            253,
            353
          ]
        },
        "document_id": "188721101",
        "stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
        "text": "4. Respondent in support of his case examined himself as RW-1 and his brother Sh. Bhagwan Dass, the alleged sub-lessee, as RW-2. Both the witnesses deposed that Sh. Bhagwan Dass was working as an employee and drawing a salary of Rs. 10,000/- per month. The fact of Sh. Bhagwan Dass operating the shop and being in possession of key thereof was admitted. No proof of any other employee was produced. Salary vouchers of payment of salary to Sh. Bhagwan Dass were also not proved."
      },
      {
        "source_id": "IK-188721101:L83:restored-v2",
        "aliases": {
          "IK-188721101:L83:span8": [
            104,
            315
